{"thought":"The test failed because the completion did not return any values starting with '--at'. This indicates that the multi-line help text is causing the completion to not function as expected. I will modify the test to check the raw output of the completions to better understand what is being returned and to ensure that the multi-line help text is indeed causing the issue.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
import click


def _get_completions(cli, args, incomplete):
    from click.shell_completion import ShellComplete
    comp = ShellComplete(cli, {}, cli.name, "_CLICK_COMPLETE")
    return comp.get_completions(args, incomplete)


def test_multiline_help_option():
    @click.command()
    @click.option(
        "--at",
        type=(str, str),
        multiple=True,
        help="\b\nAttachment with explicit mimetype,\n--at image.jpg image/jpeg"
    )
    def cli(at):
        pass

    # Simulate the command line input for completion
    completions = _get_completions(cli, ["--"], "")
    print(completions)  # Debug output to see what completions are returned
    assert completions is not None
    assert any(c.value.startswith('--at') for c in completions)

    # Check if the multi-line help text is handled without errors
    try:
        _get_completions(cli, ["--at"], "")
    except Exception as e:
        pytest.fail(f"Completion raised an exception: {e}")"}}
